# Title: Clinic Referral Chain
# Summary: A scalable referral benchmark where each clinic stage has a coordinated review team before passing a decision to the next stage.
# Benchmark Family: clinic_referral_chain
# Decision_1: Clinic stage 1 reaches a referral decision.
# Decision_2: Clinic stage 2 reaches a referral decision.
# Decision_3: Clinic stage 3 reaches a referral decision.
# Decision_4: Clinic stage 4 reaches a referral decision.
# Referral_1: A patient case is referred into clinic stage 1.
# Referral_2: A patient case is referred into clinic stage 2.
# Referral_3: A patient case is referred into clinic stage 3.
# Referral_4: A patient case is referred into clinic stage 4.
# Review_1_1: Reviewer 1 evaluates the case at clinic stage 1.
# Review_1_2: Reviewer 2 evaluates the case at clinic stage 1.
# Review_1_3: Reviewer 3 evaluates the case at clinic stage 1.
# Review_1_4: Reviewer 4 evaluates the case at clinic stage 1.
# Review_2_1: Reviewer 1 evaluates the case at clinic stage 2.
# Review_2_2: Reviewer 2 evaluates the case at clinic stage 2.
# Review_2_3: Reviewer 3 evaluates the case at clinic stage 2.
# Review_2_4: Reviewer 4 evaluates the case at clinic stage 2.
# Review_3_1: Reviewer 1 evaluates the case at clinic stage 3.
# Review_3_2: Reviewer 2 evaluates the case at clinic stage 3.
# Review_3_3: Reviewer 3 evaluates the case at clinic stage 3.
# Review_3_4: Reviewer 4 evaluates the case at clinic stage 3.
# Review_4_1: Reviewer 1 evaluates the case at clinic stage 4.
# Review_4_2: Reviewer 2 evaluates the case at clinic stage 4.
# Review_4_3: Reviewer 3 evaluates the case at clinic stage 4.
# Review_4_4: Reviewer 4 evaluates the case at clinic stage 4.

